# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML site following the official Vercel documentation.

## What Was Implemented

### 1. Added Web Analytics Script Tag
Added the Vercel Web Analytics CDN script to all 10 HTML pages:
- `<script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>`

This script was placed immediately after the existing Speed Insights script in the `<head>` section of each file.

### 2. Updated Content Security Policy
Modified `vercel.json` to allow the Vercel Analytics CDN in the Content Security Policy:
- Added `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com` to `script-src` directive
- Added `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com https://*.vercel-insights.com` to `connect-src` directive

This ensures the analytics script can load and send data without being blocked by CSP.

## Files Modified

### HTML Files (11 files):
1. `index.html` - Main landing page
2. `app.html` - Application page
3. `metodo.html` - Methodology page
4. `versoes.html` - Versions/modules page
5. `para-escritorios.html` - For offices page
6. `limitacoes.html` - Limitations page
7. `quant-ai.html` - Evidence page
8. `btech.html` - Redirect page
9. `benevente-1.html` - Redirect page
10. `benevente-2.html` - Redirect page

### Configuration Files (1 file):
1. `vercel.json` - Updated CSP headers to allow analytics CDN

## Implementation Notes

### Why This Approach?
This is a static HTML site without a package manager (npm/pnpm/yarn) or build system. According to the official Vercel documentation, the correct approach for static sites is to use the CDN script tag method rather than installing the `@vercel/analytics` npm package.

### Documentation Reference
The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics documentation:
- Quickstart guide: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Package documentation: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package

The CDN approach (`https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js`) is the recommended method for vanilla HTML/JavaScript sites.

### Existing Infrastructure
The site already had Vercel Speed Insights configured (`/_vercel/insights/script.js`). The Web Analytics script was added alongside it to provide comprehensive analytics coverage:
- **Speed Insights**: Performance metrics (Core Web Vitals)
- **Web Analytics**: Traffic analytics (page views, user behavior)

### Security Considerations
The Content Security Policy was carefully updated to maintain security while allowing analytics:
- Only the specific CDN domain is whitelisted
- The CSP remains restrictive for all other directives
- The `defer` attribute ensures scripts don't block page rendering

## Next Steps

To enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard:
1. Go to your project in Vercel Dashboard
2. Navigate to Analytics tab
3. Enable Web Analytics if not already enabled
4. Deploy this change to production
5. Verify by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/web-analytics/view`

## Verification

All changes were validated:
- ✓ All 10 HTML files contain the analytics script tag
- ✓ JSON syntax in vercel.json is valid
- ✓ HTML syntax in all modified files is valid
- ✓ CSP configuration includes necessary domains
- ✓ Script tags use `defer` attribute for optimal performance
